---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const effectiveDate = "September 20, 2026";
const contactEmail = "ncsuappdevelopmentclub@gmail.com";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — FoodFinder"
  description="FoodFinder does not collect personal information. Read the full privacy policy.">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="tagline">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>

  <p>
    FoodFinder is an app for viewing NC State Dining menus, hours, and events.
    It is developed by the Android team of the
    <a href="https://appdevncsu.org">App Development Club at NC State</a>
    (referred to below as "we", "us", or "our").
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    FoodFinder does not collect any personal information. There are no accounts,
    no advertising, and no third-party analytics or tracking. The app asks for
    only the minimum permissions it needs to work.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we do not collect</h2>
  <p>We do not collect, request, or store any of the following:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, email address, phone number, or other contact details</li>
    <li>Your location</li>
    <li>Your contacts, photos, files, or other content on your device</li>
    <li>Any account or login credentials, since the app has no accounts</li>
    <li>Advertising identifiers or any data used to track you across apps</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information handled by the app</h2>
  <p>
    The following information is handled entirely on your device and is not sent
    to us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Favorites.</strong> Menu items you mark as favorites are stored locally
      on your device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cached menus, hours, and photos.</strong> Content you view is saved
      on your device so the app works quickly and can be used offline.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Notification settings.</strong> Notifications about your favorites are
      generated on your device. We do not run a push notification service.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When you ask the app to find menus that include your favorite items, the app
    sends the <em>names of those menu items</em> (for example, "Chicken Parmesan")
    to our server so it can search the dining menus. These are food item names, not
    personal details, and they are not linked to you or your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Like most online services, our server may record standard technical
    information when the app makes a request, such as the request itself and an
    IP address. This information is used only to operate and secure the service.
    It is not used to identify you and is not shared or sold.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <p>
    We use the information described above solely to provide the app's features:
    showing dining menus, hours, and events, and helping you find your favorite
    items. We do not sell your information, and we do not share it with third
    parties for advertising or marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    FoodFinder does not include advertising, analytics, or crash-reporting SDKs.
    Menus, hours, and location photos come from publicly available NC State
    Dining sources and are delivered to the app through our own server.
  </p>
  <p>
    Requests to our server are routed through Cloudflare, which acts as a
    reverse proxy and provides security and performance features such as TLS
    termination and DDoS protection. As part of this, Cloudflare processes
    technical request information, including IP addresses, on our behalf. We do
    not use Cloudflare for advertising or analytics.
  </p>

  <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Favorites, cached content, and settings remain on your device until you
    delete them within the app or uninstall the app. Uninstalling FoodFinder
    removes this locally stored data from your device. Server logs are kept only
    as long as needed for operation and security, then deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Requests between the app and our server are sent over encrypted HTTPS
    connections.
  </p>

  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>
    FoodFinder is open source, so you can review exactly how it handles data for
    yourself. The code is available at{" "}
    <a href="https://github.com/NCSU-App-Development-Club/FoodFinder"
      >github.com/NCSU-App-Development-Club/FoodFinder</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    FoodFinder is a general-audience app and is not directed to children under
    13. Because we do not collect personal information, we do not knowingly
    collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on
    this page with a new effective date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions about this policy or about privacy in FoodFinder,
    contact us at{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    FoodFinder is not an official NC State University project. It is not
    affiliated with NC State University or Illumia (formerly Transact + CBORD,
    the company behind NetNutrition). All information displayed in the app is
    publicly available online.
  </p>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
